<title>BELGIUM: CYCLING-PROFILE OF LIEGE-BASTOGNE-LIEGE WINNER.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-PROFILE OF LIEGE-BASTOGNE-LIEGE WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>ANS, Belgium 1997-04-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of Italian Michele Bartoli, winner of the Liege-Bastogne-Liege World Cup race on Sunday:</p>
<p>Age: 26</p>
<p>Team: MG-Technogym</p>
<p>Professional debut: 1992</p>
<p>Quick facts: Born in Pisa. Started his career with the Mercantone-Uno team. Moved to MG-Technogym last year. Won his first race in 1993. Won bronze medal in 1996 world championship behind Belgian Johan Museeuw and fellow Italian Mauro Gianetti.</p>
<p>Won nine races in 1996. Liege-Bastogne-Liege is his fourth victory of 1997.</p>
<p>Leading victories: Tour of Flanders 1996, Liege-Bastogne-Liege 1997.</p>
</text>
